# config-schema.waivers — the config-stability gate's ONLY escape hatch (busbar 1.5.3, unit F).
#
# The config grammar is FROZEN after 1.5.3: additive-only forever (new OPTIONAL key / new section /
# new enum variant). `scripts/config-stability-gate.sh` fails RED on anything else. This file is the
# narrow, auditable way to say "yes, this specific break is intentional and reviewed".
#
# WHY A FILE AND NOT AN ENV VAR: an env var can be set in a workflow edit and reviewed by nobody. A
# waiver here is a line in the PR diff, sitting right next to the break it excuses, and a reviewer
# sees it. The gate also prints every applied waiver loudly in its output.
#
# RULES (enforced by scripts/config-schema.py load_waivers + proven by the gate's self-test):
#   - One waiver per line:   <exact-path> = <reason>
#     paths are  Type.field  |  Type::Variant  |  Type  |  "type AliasName"
#   - EXACT paths only. No globs, no wildcards — `*` or `?` is a hard error. A waiver excuses ONE
#     path and nothing else; any other break in the same change is still RED.
#   - A reason is MANDATORY. `path =` with no text is a hard error.
#   - A STALE waiver (one that no longer matches any break) is itself a hard error, so this file can
#     never accumulate standing permission to break something later.
#
# A waiver is a LAST RESORT. The additive path — add a NEW optional key and deprecate the old one —
# is almost always available and is what 1.5.3 froze the grammar to guarantee. If you are adding a
# line here, the change needs a human decision, not a config edit.
#
# EMPTY BY DEFAULT. It should stay that way.

# busbar 1.6.0 (owner decision 2026-09-07, "no carve outs"): a provider api_key that does not resolve
# refuses boot, and the ONE way to declare a keyless upstream is the bare scalar `none`. SecretRef
# therefore accepts that single string where it refused every string before. Registered breaking
# (shadow-oracle register F-016); every other string is still refused, proven by secret-ref tests.
manual-de SecretRef::visit_str = busbar 1.6.0 accepts the bare scalar `none` on a provider api_key (registered breaking F-016); all other inline strings stay refused
